UID:413890a2a0395832578f4d103d7e@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Art + Design\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:What is Design Next? Presented by the Museum of Design Atlanta
  in partnership with the Peachtree Branch of the Fulton County Library Sys
 tem\, Design Next is a free architecture program for students in grades 9-
 12. In this session\, we’ll explore how architects use drawing to observ
 e\, communicate\, and develop ideas. Students will practice observational 
 sketching techniques used by designers while learning how line weight\, co
 ntour drawing\, and perspective help communicate three-dimensional spaces 
 on paper. Through guided exercises and architectural sketching\, students 
 will strengthen their drawing skills while learning to see the built envir
 onment in new ways. What You’ll Do Learn why sketching \nCategory: Art +
  Design\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/design-next-seein
 g-sketching/
