DTSTAMP:20261017T153939Z
UID:1cbd099286db7f567d9fe82c68d3@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Film + TV\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:1996 | Run Time: 108 min | 35mm Directed by Spike Lee Introduc
 ed by Dr. Stephane Dunn (Morehouse College) Print provided by Yale Film Ar
 chive. GIRL 6 is Spike Lee’s eighth commercial film and the third where 
 he centers a woman as the main protagonist. Made in 1996\, it is based on 
 a play by African-American playwright Suzan-Lori Parks. It examines the ph
 one sex business (as a parody of Hollywood) and one Black woman’s dreams
  against her negotiation of that industry. Essence gushes about Theresa Ra
 ndle who stars as girl 6 saying\, “Randle possesses the chameleonlike ab
 ility to be every woman you’ve ever known and one you’ve never met bef
 ore.” Even cultural critic bell hooks\, known for getting i\nCategory: F
 ilm + TV\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/the-emory-cinema
 theque-presents-girl-6-1996/
LOCATION:White Hall 208\, 301 Dowman Dr.\, Atlanta\, GA\, 30322
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/the-emory-cinematheque-presents-girl-6-1
 996/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
