DESCRIPTION:By the end of the 17th century\, a growing middle class create
 d a demand for musical and theatrical productions\, while the availability
  of sheet music and instruments in shops resulted in a more musically-lite
 rate society. Lauda Baroque will perform selections by Henry Purcell\, Joh
 n Blow\, and George Frideric Handel—three of the central figures in 17th
  and 18th century England—while also paying homage to other composers wh
 o helped bring music to the masses. Suggested donation of $20\; no one tur
 ned away.\nCategory: Music\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/even
 t/english-masters-of-the-theater-and-court-lauda-musicam-baroque-orchestra
