BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Musical Encounters: Peruvian Viceregal Paintings — New Orleans
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-06:00":20261111T180000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-06:00":20261111T183000
DTSTAMP:20261017T153939Z
UID:57e70d7ec3811dc00c429e4e072d@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Performances\,New Orleans\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Join us for NOMA’s Musical Encounters Gallery Talk series\, 
 where local musicians and scholars host conversations connecting their pra
 ctice to works on view in the museum’s collection. This month’s Musica
 l Encounters program will be based on the presentation of Peruvian Vicereg
 al paintings\, found on the second floor Arts of the Americas galleries. I
 ncluded with museum admission\, which is free for Louisiana residents ever
 y Wednesday courtesy of The Helis Foundation’s Art for All initiative. W
 hen you arrive at NOMA\, check in at the admissions desk for directions to
  the appropriate location. No registration is required for this event seri
 es. About the Speaker More information about this Musical \nCategory: Perf
 ormances\nOriginal listing: https://noma.org/event/musical-encounters-nove
 mber-11/
LOCATION:New Orleans Museum of Art\, 1 Collins Diboll Cir\, New Orleans\, 
 LA 70124
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://noma.org/event/musical-encounters-november-11/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:noma
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Emory Cinematheque Presents: SUMMER OF SAM (1999) — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261111T193000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261111T223000
DTSTAMP:20261017T153939Z
UID:bb568edbb0ba603882752a9d4a66@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Film + TV\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Introduced by Dr. Racquel Gates (Columbia University) Released
  in 1999\, Spike Lee’s SUMMER OF SAM is based on the 1977 killing spree 
 of David Berkowitz\, known as the Son of Sam. It fuses that year’s heatw
 ave\, Bronx\, New York energy\, sex\, and disco with the fear of a serial 
 killer. It’s Lee’s first film not about Black communities. Mike Imperi
 oli (of THE SOPRANOS fame)\, Victor Colicchio\, and Lee wrote SUMMER OF SA
 M. Actor and star Roger Guenveur Smith talks about the making of the film.
  “’Summer of Sam’ was shot almost entirely in the Country Club secti
 on of the Bronx where the first of the murders took place. ‘You could fe
 el it among the people on the street who had actually lived through th\nCa
 tegory: Film + TV\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/the-emo
 ry-cinematheque-presents-summer-of-sam-1999/
LOCATION:White Hall 208\, 301 Dowman Dr.\, Atlanta\, GA\, 30322
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/the-emory-cinematheque-presents-summer-o
 f-sam-1999/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
